  "prefLabel": "Nur 701.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2006-12-21",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 701.01 Purpose. These rules set forth requirements pursuant to RSA 326-B:9 and RSA 326-B:32 requiring nursing assistant training and competency testing. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act (OBRA) of 1987; Section 1819 and 1919 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1395 & 1396) and RSA 326-B authorize a registry that lists all nursing assistants who qualify through education and testing to provide nursing-related activities.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Nur 100) #5887, eff 8-26-94; ss by #6778, eff 6-26-98; ss by #8664, INTERIM, eff 6-24-06, EXPIRED: 12-21-06\n\nNew. #8873, eff 4-24-07; ss by #10302, eff 3-22-13; ss by #10570, eff 4-17-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nur100-800.html"
